    "created_at": "2016-04-20T21:39:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-20T21:40:30Z",
    "body": "Because the browser processes the event loop in a loop, and if there are outstanding tasks still queued there it probably shouldn't start doing focus-related stuff? I guess that's kind of weak.\n\nIn any case, your example doesn't work since only author-initiated focus changes trigger the `change` event. It would have to be some scenario where the browser processes the event loop so slowly that a user can actually take the time between the queuing of the fire-`input` task, and the execution of the fire-`input` task, to press \"tab\" and move their focus.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/212618165/reactions",
